## Ownership matrix

| Responsibility | Owner |
|---|---|
| Product and architecture direction, major decisions | {{OWNER_ROLE}} |
| Roadmap, Goal, Work Spec, Plan review, acceptance, PROGRESS | {{SUPERVISOR_AGENT}} |
| Plan, implementation, tests and validation, Result, tactical workers | {{IMPLEMENTER_AGENT}} |

## Management structure

Goal artifacts live in `management/{{RELEASE}}/` (`goals/`, `specs/`, `plans/`, `results/`, `archive/`) with stable
IDs (`G###`) that are never reused. Revisions preserve history. PROGRESS is the mutable index; BACKLOG holds
proposals, not authorization. The release-independent supervisor reference is
[SUPERVISOR-HANDOFF](management/SUPERVISOR-HANDOFF.md). Goals carry the eleven fields in order; Specs, Plans and
Results follow the formats in the roles reference.

Only final ACCEPT completes a Goal. Plan approval, readiness and conditional integration are distinct earlier
states. Formal reviews return exactly one of **ACCEPT**, **CORRECTION LOOP** or **ARCHITECTURE DECISION REQUIRED**.

For failed-batch/correction handoffs, use the
[compact repair checklist](.agents/skills/sdlc-management/references/coordination.md#compact-repair-handoff).
Reference exact source/diff, focused evidence, tried fixes, hypothesis and next test
in existing Result/review records. No full-log payload or separate packet required.

## Bounded specification authority and owner stop boundaries

Automatic continuation stops at a missing Spec unless {{OWNER_ROLE}} explicitly
authorizes {{SUPERVISOR_AGENT}} to write Goals/Specs within a recorded named
inclusive endpoint, task set/range or pinned epic. Record the owner instruction,
roadmap commit/task membership, start, allowed phases, endpoint and stop/resume
authority in existing PROGRESS/handoff records. No implicit expansion or new registry.
Specification-only mandates stop at docs; full-epic delivery mandates retain
separate Goal budgets and every review/dependency/binding/permission/barrier gate.
Independent owner stops override continuation even with ready Specs/approved
Plans; check before advance planning during CI. "Stop before G013" excludes it;
"finish G013 then stop" includes closeout but no successor planning. Clarify an
ambiguous "stop at/next task" before crossing it. Pause out-of-bound work safely,
preserve artifacts and owner decision history, and never skip to a later task.
See [mandates and stops](.agents/skills/sdlc-management/references/roles-lifecycle.md#bounded-specification-authority-and-owner-stop-boundaries).

